# Keep the build context small and reproducible.
.git
.gitignore
.venv
venv
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

.env
deploy/
# HB-111: the models image (SLAB, its build gate and Dockerfile) is a second image beside the
# server, never part of it. `deploy/` above already holds it; named here so the fence stands if
# that line is ever narrowed. test_container_image.py (a test held privately) holds both.
deploy/models/
eval/
tests/
.github/
.agents/

.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# The pack build's local artifacts (gitignored; 34 MB on a workstation). The runtime reads
# packs/*.json only (src/hazbrief/packs.py); a build from a checkout never holds them.
packs/build/

# The application (DN-010 D2, DN-011 section 3; HB-87R): the evidence store, the brief and
# the first-order puff (DN-018), a client of the server that the server never imports. The
# image is the server alone. `src/hazbrief/command.py` stays: it is the `hazbrief` console
# entry and imports the application only inside `hazbrief brief`. The three packs below are
# the puff's (`hazbrief.models.APP_PACK_MODELS`), read only by `packs.load_app_pack`.
# test_container_image.py (a test held privately) builds the image's file list and holds all of this.
src/hazbrief/brief/
src/hazbrief/evidence/
packs/materials_properties.json
packs/sigma_curves.json
packs/release_scenarios.json
# HB-120: the brief's release routing table (every ERG guide to a release model or to "no dispersion model applies"),
# read only by `packs.load_app_pack`, and its authored source.
packs/release_routing.json
packs/src/release_routing.yaml
# HB-155: the brief's siting rules (the command post, triage and staging; DN-023), read only by
# `packs.load_app_pack`, and its authored source.
packs/siting_rules.json
packs/src/siting_rules.yaml
# HB-119: the brief's materials resolver's threshold tables (built from the held AEGL table and NIOSH Pocket Guide) and
# its runtime cache of fetched entries (gitignored, written on a workstation by any brief that resolves a material).
packs/src/thresholds_*.json
packs/cache/
# HB-128: the PM2.5 AQI categories, breakpoints and messages the smoke layer will read (DN-021 section 4); the
# application's, never the server's.
packs/src/aqi_pm25_breakpoints.json
